// case: kernel/sum_bound_plain_add
// clause: SPEC-01 IM-77 (an exact sum, one final range check); SPEC-02 K-1, F-5 check 5 (a `where` bound holds at every item)
// subset: cint-core-1 (kernel)
// entry: run; args: none
// spec outcome: value I64 2147483653. The two kernels sum exactly; the first's bound (n <= 16, I32 elements: at most 2^35 in magnitude) lets an implementation add without a per-element check, the second's I64 elements pass through 2^63 twice on the way to 0. Issue 541

kernel bounded[n](in I32[n] x, out I64 s) over [i: n] where n <= 16 {
    reduce s = sum(x[i]);
}

kernel unbounded[n](in I64[n] x, out I64 s) over [i: n] {
